Package: corrInspect
Type: Package
Title: Correlation Inspector
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-08-23
Authors@R: c(person("Ravi", "Selker", role=c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Jonathon", "Love", role=c("aut", "cph"), email="jon@thon.cc"),
    person("Damian", "Dropmann", role=c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Victor", "Moreno", role=c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email="v.moreno@iconcologia.net"))
Maintainer: Victor Moreno <v.moreno@iconcologia.net>
Description: A clone of jmv's Correlation Matrix analysis, redesigned for
    cleaner output. Instead of a sparse n-by-n matrix table, results are
    presented as a tidy one-row-per-pair table (with the 95% CI collapsed
    into a single cell instead of separate columns), which naturally reduces
    to a single row when only two variables are analysed. A second mode
    ("one variable vs. the rest") compares a chosen reference variable
    against several others, for inspecting candidate predictors or
    confounders before a regression. Scatterplots are annotated in place
    with r, its 95% CI, and the fitted regression line, and the all-vs-all
    overview is a colour-coded heatmap rather than a plain-text matrix.
